+
+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* can also declare a default value for an argument. The value the
+*hookimpl* receives for such an argument is, in order of precedence:
+
+1. the value passed by the hook call,
+2. the :ref:`default value declared by the hookspec <hookspec_arg_default>`,
+3. the default value declared by the *hookimpl* itself.
+
+The *hookimpl* default is therefore only used when neither the caller nor the
+*hookspec* provide the argument. This allows a plugin to use a new hook
+argument while staying compatible with older versions of the host program
+whose *hookspec* does not have the argument yet:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="fallback"):
+        print(new_arg)
+
+
+    # Prints "get this".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args, new_arg="get this")
+    # Prints the hookspec default if the hookspec declares one for new_arg,
+    # otherwise "fallback".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args)
+
+This applies to all kinds of *hookimpls*, including
+:ref:`wrappers <hookwrappers>`.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+    A value passed by the hook call, or a hookspec default, now takes
+    precedence over the default value declared by the *hookimpl*. Previously
+    the *hookimpl* default was always used.
 
 
